From 7d22ee045ff390a3a18c70f1ba55be3afecfdc57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bandersong <134746909+bandersong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:46:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/26] 0001 CHOP: send each pad's note-off to the track its
 note-on went to

The note-on now records, per pad, whether it was rewritten to the chop
track (chop_route[12], RAM, power-on 0xFF). The note-off of that pad is
rewritten only when its note-on was, and the record is then cleared, so
turning CHP while a pad is held can no longer split a note-on and its
note-off across two tracks (TRUTH D8a). Pad ids above 11 touch no table
and stay stock.

design.md: CHOP is for the normal pad mode; turn CHP OFF before using
chromatic, scale or other pad modes (D14). Path-by-path check of both pad
gates in the built image, every differing region with its owner, and a
founder test card: control first, then the CHOP build, recovery steps,
and note-off checks. make chop, chop-min and control PASS in the guest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
