 (D21)

- H STR (id 2: an Error-class record, 0008's HCT, not in image A; id 7 was
  rejected in step 3): OFF, 1, 2, 4 ... 64 steps. A change while CHOP is on
  writes the chop track's LFO through chop_put (param_set_value, record 0,
  notify 1): DST = STA (0x1500), WAV RMP, MOD ONE, SPH 0, FAD 0x4000, SPD
  0x6000, MUL (7 - idx) << 8, DEP 0x7fff (full, constant), END 0x7800, LOP 0;
  OFF writes DST none and DEP 0x4000. CHOP off: the value is stored only.
  No RETRIG write. The speed rule 2048 / (SPD * MUL) is unverified.
- lock_gate gives STR its own held-path branch (the same turn, base values
  only, returns 0), so a held trig never makes a stock p-lock for id 2.
- STR's value rows sit in .text (cave2 is full: 31 B left).

Guest: make samplefocus, chop-min, control, verify, random PASS. CHOP: .text
1216 B in cave (16 free), .cave2 1433 B (31 free); 0 bytes changed in the
bootstrap; image sha256 39a01d5a...a5c3, .syx 02fd3e60...f498.

