From: bandersong <134746909+bandersong@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 14:21:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/26] Image B step 5 (D29 option 4, part a):
 behaviour-identical compaction of CHOP

Image A' (make samplefocus) shrinks by 186 B with the same stock calls and the
same arguments on every path; the one visible change is the CHOP STA dial.

- chop_set_sta is a 12-byte tail into chop_put (id 43, record 1): chop_put was
  the same body for any id and record flag.
- dial_gate and its detour at 0x400a587c are gone (D29): the CHOP STA knob's
  dial is id 4's own again; 0x400a587c is stock in every 0001 build.
- chop_set_of: the project -> kit -> track set lookup chop_put and
  chop_held_with each made inline (same three calls, same order).
- chop_locked: the four inline "can this id be p-locked now" tests
  (param_info(id), bit 8) in chop_held_with and chop_lay.
- chop_end_put: the common tail of chop_end_hit and chop_end_restore.
- pad_on_gate keeps the marker in d3 (dead at that detour, saved by every
  helper) instead of reloading chop_pad/chop_marks after chop_held_lock.

0001 .text 1128 -> 1040 B, .cave2 1305 -> 1207 B; 0000-shared unchanged.
Guest: samplefocus PASS (syx bf89fed2..., MAIN OS e96dd2fb...), chop-min,
control, verify (0c134c6c..., unchanged), random (1de1f98c..., unchanged),
guard-check PASS. Symbol-by-symbol compare against cef0828's A': 48 symbols
identical, 7 changed exactly as above, 0 other bytes; receipts in
corp/r7b-builder/a2/ (compare_b0_a2.txt, prove_a.txt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
