Subject: [PATCH 25/26] r7b integrator: panel corrections (verify gate-aware,
 image B card, cave3 notes)

Every image is unchanged; rebuilt in the guest with the same hashes (image B
86e1dd1b..., image A' 23a20937..., verify 0d51f7cb..., random 3dafc0bd...,
control 3407638c...), all PASS.

- tools/verify.py (panel b1): the claim check counts only the claims of the
  mods the build contains (manifest mods / detours / patches), selected by the
  gates and params in the manifest; the displaced-bytes search uses the same
  claims. Before, every registry claim counted, so a byte written into a
  gated-out claim or another mod's claim passed and verify named the wrong
  owners (image B: 0001's gates and .chst were reported as 0008's or 0002's).
  Negative test in a guest temp copy: a byte flipped at a 0004 detour site in
  image B, or inside 0008's claim in image A', is now UNCLAIMED / FAIL where the
  old verify said "ok".
- tools/build.py (panel b1): a detour's target is checked against the owner's
  active claims only.
- registry + design.md (panel F1/PB5/b2): cave3's notes said no audio-interrupt
  code is there, but cut_process calls coefs (cave3, top 512 B) four times from
  the audio interrupt, as 0008 was always built. The notes now say so: the
  audio path's entry and body stay in cave; coefs and cut_coef stay in cave3 and
  are only read; nothing in cave3 is written at run time.
- design.md image B card: S4 runs before any kit is saved with LCT/HCT on, with
  the way back (LCT 0 / HCT 127 everywhere, save, image A') and no measuring
  build on B (panel F2); S9 and H11's CHOP-OFF clause warn that the held trig is
  released as a hold with no edit (panel PB2, r6 gate G1); S10 turns CHP OFF to
  select the second track and back ON to re-latch T (PB3); the page operations
  (old S2 tail, S7) and MIDI CC (S8) run last, after saving (PB4).
- docs/MANUAL.md + README.md (panel PB1, repo part): on branch chop the images
  to flash are image A' and image B, not the make verify / make random builds;
  image B has no measuring build; LCT/HCT cannot be p-locked or scene-assigned
  (r5b pages skeptic housekeeping). The founder's flash/ folder is not touched.

